## Why This Is Asked
Evaluates expertise in real-time blind source separation for production telemetry systems, combining theoretical signal processing with practical systems engineering under edge computing constraints.

## Key Concepts
- Online ICA and whitening for streaming data processing
- Adaptive forgetting mechanisms for nonstationary source tracking
- Temporal permutation resolution across sliding windows
- Edge infrastructure latency and computational optimization
- Validation methodology using synthetic ground-truth injection

## Code Example
```javascript
// Online Infomax-like ICA implementation
function onlineICA(whitenedData, learningRate) {
  // Initialize separation matrix
  let W = initializeMatrix();

  return function update(newSample) {
    // Natural gradient update
    const y = W * newSample;
    const g = tanh(y);
    const delta = learningRate * (g * newSample - (1 - g * g) * W);

    // Update separation matrix
    W += delta;
    return y;
  };
}
```

## Why This Is Asked

Car environments introduce dynamic geometry, intermittent sensor faults, and real-time constraints. This question probes the ability to design an online ICA solution that adapts to changing mixing, handles missing data gracefully, and maintains consistent source order over time.

## Key Concepts

- Online sliding-window ICA with adaptive whitening
- Kalman-style demixer updates on whitened data
- Missing-channel handling via subspace completion without reinitialization
- Permutation stability using short temporal memory and cross-frame non-Gaussianity cues
- Real-time latency targets and robust evaluation (ground-truth SDR/SIR, perceptual checks)

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudocode: online update for W on whitened data Xw
function onlineUpdate(W, Xw, lr) {
  const Y = W.dot(Xw);
  const e = gradientNonGaussianity(Y);
  return W.add(e.mul(lr).dot(Xw.transpose()));
}
```

